kanon lean-all DIR writes the Lean files that it generates for the root R of a
module under DIR/R/Generated/, and the hand-written files of R go beside that
directory (DIR/R/Sem.lean, DIR/R/Proofs.lean, ...). Everything under a
Generated directory is generated, and nothing outside is written by kanon.

  $ kanon lean-all out lang.knl
  $ ls out/Ex out/Ex/Int
  out/Ex:
  Generated
  Int
  
  out/Ex/Int:
  Generated
  $ find out/Ex/Int -type f | sort
  out/Ex/Int/Generated/Lang.lean
  out/Ex/Int/Generated/Lift.lean
  out/Ex/Int/Generated/Model.lean
  out/Ex/Int/Generated/Node.lean
  out/Ex/Int/Generated/Soundness.lean
  out/Ex/Int/Generated/Soundness/Comm.lean
  out/Ex/Int/Generated/Soundness/Int/neg.lean
  out/Ex/Int/Generated/Soundness/Int/plus.lean
  out/Ex/Int/Generated/Statements/Comm.lean
  out/Ex/Int/Generated/Statements/Int/neg.lean
  out/Ex/Int/Generated/Statements/Int/plus.lean
  $ head -n 3 out/Ex/Generated/Rules.lean
  -- Generated by kanon from lang.knl, int.knl. Do not edit.
  import Ex.Generated.Semantics
  import Ex.Int.Generated.Soundness

A hand-written file beside Generated is imported by the generated ones, and is
never touched.

  $ echo 'import Ex.Int.Generated.Node' > out/Ex/Int/Sem.lean
  $ echo '-- A file of mine.' > out/Ex/Mine.lean
  $ kanon lean-all out lang.knl
  $ grep '^import Ex.Int.Sem' out/Ex/Int/Generated/Lang.lean
  import Ex.Int.Sem
  $ cat out/Ex/Int/Sem.lean out/Ex/Mine.lean
  import Ex.Int.Generated.Node
  -- A file of mine.

With --check, kanon lean-all checks that Generated has exactly the files that it
would write, and nothing else.

  $ kanon lean-all --check out lang.knl

A file that is missing, one that was edited, and any other file, of any name,
whatever its first line, are reported.

  $ rm out/Ex/Generated/Rules.lean
  $ echo '-- edited' >> out/Ex/Generated/Syntax.lean
  $ mkdir -p out/Ex/Generated/Old
  $ echo '-- Generated by kanon from int.kn. Do not edit.' > out/Ex/Generated/Old/Gone.lean
  $ echo 'mine' > out/Ex/Generated/notes.txt
  $ kanon lean-all --check out lang.knl
  kanon: out/Ex/Generated/Syntax.lean is not up to date (run kanon lean-all)
  kanon: out/Ex/Generated/Rules.lean is missing (run kanon lean-all)
  kanon: out/Ex/Generated/Old/Gone.lean is no longer generated (run kanon lean-all)
  kanon: out/Ex/Generated/notes.txt is no longer generated (run kanon lean-all)
  [1]

kanon lean-all removes the whole Generated directory before it writes it again,
but nothing else.

  $ kanon lean-all out lang.knl
  $ kanon lean-all --check out lang.knl
  $ ls out/Ex out/Ex/Generated
  out/Ex:
  Generated
  Int
  Mine.lean
  
  out/Ex/Generated:
  Lang.lean
  Lift.lean
  Model.lean
  Node.lean
  Rules.lean
  Semantics.lean
  Soundness.lean
  Syntax.lean
  $ cat out/Ex/Int/Sem.lean out/Ex/Mine.lean
  import Ex.Int.Generated.Node
  -- A file of mine.

The files are the same, byte for byte, when Generated is deleted and written
again.

  $ cp -r out out.bak
  $ rm -r out/Ex/Generated out/Ex/Int/Generated
  $ kanon lean-all --check out lang.knl 2>&1 | head -n 2
  kanon: out/Ex/Generated/Node.lean is missing (run kanon lean-all)
  kanon: out/Ex/Generated/Lang.lean is missing (run kanon lean-all)
  $ kanon lean-all out lang.knl
  $ diff -r out out.bak

A function or a rule that is removed leaves no stale file.

  $ mkdir fewer && cp lang.knl int.knl fewer && sed '/^rule neg/,$d' int.kn > fewer/int.kn
  $ kanon lean-all --check out fewer/lang.knl 2>&1 | grep neg
  kanon: out/Ex/Int/Generated/Soundness/Int/neg.lean is no longer generated (run kanon lean-all)
  kanon: out/Ex/Int/Generated/Statements/Int/neg.lean is no longer generated (run kanon lean-all)
  $ kanon lean-all out fewer/lang.knl
  $ find out -name 'neg.lean' -o -name 'Sem.lean' -o -name 'Mine.lean' | sort
  out/Ex/Int/Sem.lean
  out/Ex/Mine.lean
  $ kanon lean-all --check out fewer/lang.knl
  $ kanon lean-all out2 fewer/lang.knl
  $ echo '-- Generated by kanon from int.kn. Do not edit.' > out2/Ex/Generated/Removed.lean
  $ kanon lean-all out2 fewer/lang.knl
  $ ls out2/Ex/Generated
  Lang.lean
  Lift.lean
  Model.lean
  Node.lean
  Rules.lean
  Semantics.lean
  Soundness.lean
  Syntax.lean

The roots that are not generated are not touched, even if they have a Generated
directory.

  $ mkdir -p out2/Other/Generated && echo x > out2/Other/Generated/x.lean
  $ kanon lean-all out2 fewer/lang.knl
  $ cat out2/Other/Generated/x.lean
  x

kanon lean-all does not delete through a symbolic link, nor a file: it fails
before it writes or deletes anything.

  $ mkdir elsewhere && echo precious > elsewhere/file
  $ rm -r out2/Ex/Generated && ln -s ../../elsewhere out2/Ex/Generated
  $ kanon lean-all out2 fewer/lang.knl
  kanon: out2/Ex/Generated is a symbolic link: kanon does not follow it
  [1]
  $ kanon lean-all --check out2 fewer/lang.knl
  kanon: out2/Ex/Generated is a symbolic link: kanon does not follow it
  [1]
  $ cat elsewhere/file
  precious
  $ ls elsewhere
  file
  $ rm out2/Ex/Generated && echo x > out2/Ex/Generated
  $ kanon lean-all out2 fewer/lang.knl
  kanon: out2/Ex/Generated is not a directory
  [1]
  $ cat out2/Ex/Generated
  x
  $ rm out2/Ex/Generated && mkdir out2/Ex/Generated
  $ mv out2/Ex out2/Ex.real && ln -s Ex.real out2/Ex
  $ kanon lean-all out2 fewer/lang.knl
  kanon: out2/Ex is a symbolic link: kanon does not follow it
  [1]
  $ rm out2/Ex && mv out2/Ex.real out2/Ex

A symbolic link inside Generated is removed, not followed.

  $ ln -s ../../../elsewhere out2/Ex/Generated/link
  $ kanon lean-all --check out2 fewer/lang.knl 2>&1 | grep link
  kanon: out2/Ex/Generated/link is no longer generated (run kanon lean-all)
  $ kanon lean-all out2 fewer/lang.knl
  $ ls elsewhere out2/Ex/Generated
  elsewhere:
  file
  
  out2/Ex/Generated:
  Lang.lean
  Lift.lean
  Model.lean
  Node.lean
  Rules.lean
  Semantics.lean
  Soundness.lean
  Syntax.lean

DIR is a directory, and is created if it does not exist, as there is nothing to
delete then. A root has no part called Generated, which would put hand-written
files under a Generated directory.

  $ echo x > afile
  $ kanon lean-all afile fewer/lang.knl
  kanon: afile is not a directory
  [1]
  $ kanon lean-all --check newdir fewer/lang.knl 2>&1 | head -n 1
  kanon: newdir/Ex/Generated/Node.lean is missing (run kanon lean-all)
  $ test -e newdir || echo not created
  not created
  $ printf '[@@@lean_root "Ex.Generated"]\nsort TA\nnode A of int : TA\n' > gen.knl
  $ kanon lean-all out3 gen.knl
  kanon: the root "Ex.Generated" of the module Gen has a part called Generated
  [1]
  $ test -e out3 || echo nothing written
  nothing written
